# Performance Skill

Reference with **@claude-skills/performance** when optimizing or analyzing performance.

## When to use

- User reports slowness or asks for optimization
- Improving throughput, latency, or resource use
- Designing for scale (async, pooling, caching, batching)

## Principles

- Measure or reason about bottlenecks before changing code (profiling, metrics, N+1, etc.)
- Prefer async and connection pooling for I/O-bound work; align with project patterns
- Use caching (e.g. Redis) where appropriate; respect cache invalidation
- Keep DB queries minimal and indexed; avoid N+1 and large unbounded results
- Document trade-offs (e.g. memory vs CPU, consistency vs speed) when relevant
